Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=2: texture handles and storage buffer pointers read from constant buffers at a draw also come from a page's copy; the guard takes the pages of three frames back by default; counts the pages its guess missed

T88, batch t88-a (door walk): the copy mode kept the speed (control 20.2 16.8 14.7 20.9 fps per
5 s, copy 19.3 16.1 14.8 20.5) and cut the glitches (control 3 / 3 moments; copy 0 / 1), but one
copy run still had the over-bright frame at the cut and a fade out of order, and with
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_ALWAYS it had 11 moments, where the waiting guard had none. The waiting guard
stops a writer thread for good, so it also covers what the copies do not: reads that do not go
through BufferCache::ReadGuestForBuffer, and pages the guess from earlier frames missed.

- AheadGuard::ReadGpu: the six storage buffer pointer and size reads in the buffer cache and the
  texture handle reads of the graphics and compute pipelines take a copied page's bytes from its
  copy. A lock-free bit per page says whether a page has a copy, so only those reads take the
  guard's lock.
- EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_SETS defaults to 14 (one, two and three presents back; was 6): Ocarina
  presents three images in turn, and its per-frame memory may follow them.
- The log line adds: of the pages a frame first read with its guard up, how many were not in
  the guard (the guess missed them: a guest write there goes unseen).

---
